# ============================================================
# Tools4Genz — Frontend Environment Configuration
# ============================================================
#
# These variables are public (safe to commit). They control the
# Cloudflare Worker API base URL that the frontend uses for
# request submission and status lookup.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE_URL
#   Development:  http://localhost:8787
#     (the default port wrangler dev uses; adjust if you set a custom port)
#
#   Production:   https://api.tools4genz.com
#     (replace with your actual deployed Worker custom domain)
#
#   Fallback:     /api
#     When left unset, the frontend falls back to relative-path routing.
#     This works when the project is deployed to Cloudflare Pages with
#     the wrangler.toml routes config active (see worker/wrangler.toml).
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Example:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
#
#   Or for production deployment:
#   VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.tools4genz.com
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Note:
#   • The VITE_ prefix is required by Vite for environment variable exposure.
#   • Only public, non-secret configuration belongs here.
#   • API keys, database credentials, and secret tokens must NEVER be
#     exposed through VITE_ variables.
# ============================================================
VITE_API_BASE_URL=